---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Brand from "../components/Brand.astro";
import HeadlineMotion from "../components/HeadlineMotion.astro";
import CallActions from "../components/CallActions.astro";
import { PHONE_DISPLAY, TEL_URL } from "../data/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="YardUluv Founders Club"
  description="Landscaping companies that take part before YardUluv goes on sale to everyone get founder pricing for life, locked for as long as they stay members. Members get setup and sales training in person."
>
  <div class="container page">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">
        <Brand /> · In development
      </p>
      <h1>
        <HeadlineMotion effect="rise" lines={["The Founders Club."]} />
      </h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Every landscaping company that takes part before <Brand /> goes on sale
        to everyone joins the Founders Club and keeps founder pricing for life,
        locked for as long as they stay members.
      </p>
      <CallActions />
    </header>
    <div class="club-grid">
      <section class="section" aria-labelledby="get-heading">
        <h2 id="get-heading">What you get</h2>
        <ul class="benefits">
          <li>
            <strong>Founder pricing for life</strong>, locked at the monthly
            price you join at for as long as you stay a member. Your written
            terms spell out exactly what that covers.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Setup at your shop.</strong> Charles comes to you and sets
            you up in person.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Your price list, built with you.</strong> Charles builds it
            with you now and loads it into <Brand /> as that part is ready.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Estimates built for you.</strong> Until <Brand /> can price
            your jobs, Charles builds itemized estimates for real jobs you’re
            bidding, from your price list. Your written terms say how many.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Sales training, in person.</strong> A working session with
            you and your salespeople: how to walk a customer through an itemized
            price at the kitchen table.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Each piece as it’s ready.</strong> Members try every part
            first, starting with the property model.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>A direct line.</strong> Call or text Charles at{" "}
            <a href={TEL_URL} set:text={PHONE_DISPLAY} />.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>
      <section class="section" aria-labelledby="ask-heading">
        <h2 id="ask-heading">What we ask</h2>
        <ul class="benefits">
          <li>
            Show Charles how you price a job today. One quote that went well and
            one that went sideways is plenty.
          </li>
          <li>
            About 30&nbsp;minutes every two weeks to tell us what works and what
            doesn’t.
          </li>
          <li>
            One <span class="nobr">ride-along</span> on a sales visit, with your
            customer’s OK.
          </li>
          <li>Straight answers. If something is wrong or slow, say so.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          These are requests, not conditions. Once you have a founder price,
          it’s never taken away for not helping enough.
        </p>
        <p>
          Not ready to pay? You can still help build it. Charles will tell you
          in writing what that takes and how your founder price is held.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="for-heading">
      <h2 id="for-heading">Who it’s for</h2>
      <p>
        Landscaping companies in Northeast Ohio that sell install work: beds,
        plantings, sod, patios and walls. Kent, Akron, Cleveland, Canton,
        Youngstown and the towns between.
      </p>
      <p>
        Charles sets up each company himself, so he takes on a few at a time.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="stands-heading">
      <h2 id="stands-heading">Where it stands</h2>
      <p>
        <Brand /> is in development. Today we can build a 3D model of a property
        from public mapping data and measure on it, and Charles will show you.
        Designing, pricing and the proposal are being built now.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/yarduluv/#where-it-stands">
        See what works today <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </section>
    <section class="section faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
      <h2 id="faq-heading">Questions</h2>
      <details>
        <summary>What does it cost?</summary>
        <p>
          Membership is a monthly subscription that starts when you join, before
          <Brand /> is finished. Until it’s ready, it pays for the setup visit,
          your price list, the estimates Charles builds for you and the sales
          training. After that, it’s <Brand /> itself, at the same price.
          Charles goes over the price with you in person and gives you every
          term in writing before you pay anything.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Why join before it’s finished?</summary>
        <p>
          You lock in the founder price, and how you actually sell shapes what
          gets built. Charles would rather hear what’s wrong from you now than
          after it’s done.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How far will Charles drive?</summary>
        <p>Anywhere in Northeast Ohio. If you’re farther out, call anyway.</p>
      </details>
    </section>
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="join-heading">
      <h2 id="join-heading">Ask about joining</h2>
      <ol class="join">
        <li>
          Call or text Charles at <a href={TEL_URL} set:text={PHONE_DISPLAY} />.
        </li>
        <li>
          He comes to your shop, hears how you price jobs now and shows you the
          property model.
        </li>
        <li>If it’s a fit, you get the terms in writing before you decide.</li>
      </ol>
      <CallActions />
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  /* The grid carries the section gap: its margin collapses with the intro's, as on other
     pages, while the sections' own margins inside the grid would add to it. */
  .club-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    column-gap: var(--s12);
    margin-top: var(--section-gap);
  }
  .club-grid > .section {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .benefits,
  .join {
    margin: var(--s4) 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .benefits li,
  .join li {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-top: var(--s3);
  }
  .benefits strong {
    color: var(--text);
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .club-grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 0;
    }
    .club-grid > .section + .section {
      margin-top: var(--section-gap);
    }
  }
</style>
